                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are these expected?  These generally only occur on shutdown, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                        "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                        "username": "sramyagit"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net they occur during reloading time also"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is any process reloading outside of an error?  (answer in your commit message).\n\nIs this something we need to start doing everywhere, or is this a specific case?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                        "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                        "username": "sramyagit"
                    },
                    "message": "These errors are observed during normal operation (e.g. transient\nDBus states or service restarts) and do not indicate a functional\nfailure. Logging them as warnings creates unnecessary noise and\nconfusion when accessing the User Management UI."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do you care about warning errors? \nHow is transient DBus states or service restarts a problem for warning errors?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                        "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                        "username": "sramyagit"
                    },
                    "message": "Warnings should flag real issues, not expected behavior. Transient D\u2011Bus errors like io_error and EBADR during service startup are normal.\nSuppressing these keeps logs clean."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "ERROR and CRITICAL should flag real issues. WARNING is for things that might be a problem. D\u2011Bus errors like io_error and EBADR sound exactly like that, \"might only be an error in certain scenarios\"\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/9ad2c6f422bc0860314b853c287283dcbd29430d/DEVELOPING.md?plain=1#L228C1-L230C58\n\n\n```\n- warning: A condition occurred that is outside the expected flows, but isn't\n  necessarily an error in the webserver, or might only be an error in certain\n  scenarios. For example, connection drops or 4xx errors.\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> transient DBus states or service restarts\n\nThis isn't an answer.  Services (especially phosphor-user-manager) should not be restarting randomly and making these APIs return errors, so having errors in the logs on unexpected failures is intended.  If services are returning errors randomly, that's a bug that needs fixed at the source, and bmcweb should log it to make it clear.\n\n> not expected behavior.\n\nWhere is it documented that randomized error messages and service restarts is expected?\n\n> Suppressing these keeps logs clean.\n\nAt the expense of covering up real bugs that might have impact in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                        "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                        "username": "sramyagit"
                    },
                    "message": "while enabling phosphor-ldap-config that warning got fixed. It's going to enable depends on dependency"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
